1
00:00:00,166 --> 00:00:01,432
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,433 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:04,713
Yeong Ju, thanks for today.

4
00:00:04,774 --> 00:00:05,791
Can we come again sometime?

5
00:00:05,815 --> 00:00:08,241
Hey, smile. You're a newlywed.

6
00:00:09,521 --> 00:00:12,135
- Let's go. I'll see you!
- Okay.

7
00:00:15,379 --> 00:00:16,379
Yeong Ju.

8
00:00:17,292 --> 00:00:20,060
I'll take them out for dinner.

9
00:00:20,085 --> 00:00:23,439
I'm taking them out for your sake.

10
00:00:23,673 --> 00:00:25,841
- Aren't you grateful?
- Yeah, thanks.

11
00:00:26,412 --> 00:00:27,875
Then please clean up after them.

12
00:01:11,292 --> 00:01:13,375
- Yeong Ju.
- General.

13
00:01:14,138 --> 00:01:15,331
What happened to the house?

14
00:01:16,945 --> 00:01:20,207
Sun Kyung's friends came over
and just left.

15
00:01:20,232 --> 00:01:22,877
- I'll clean up and make you dinner.
- No, that's okay.

16
00:01:23,455 --> 00:01:27,089
But if they're my wife's friends,
aren't they your friends too?

17
00:01:27,457 --> 00:01:30,870
No. It's been so long
since I saw them that it was awkward.

18
00:01:31,344 --> 00:01:33,337
Just wait a bit. I'll be quick.

19
00:01:35,679 --> 00:01:38,608
How about we go out for dinner?

20
00:01:39,359 --> 00:01:40,359
Yes.

21
00:01:43,638 --> 00:01:44,815
What have you been doing?

22
00:01:44,839 --> 00:01:46,593
You haven't even cleaned the house.

23
00:01:47,438 --> 00:01:49,987
- If you don't know, don't say anything.
- What don't I know?

24
00:01:50,012 --> 00:01:51,922
Looks like you spent all day having fun.

25
00:01:51,947 --> 00:01:53,564
So you just sit around at home...

26
00:01:54,129 --> 00:01:55,408
Shut up.

27
00:01:55,433 --> 00:01:57,707
You don't even know
what I have to put up with.

28
00:01:57,732 --> 00:01:58,932
Are you even my brother?

29
00:01:58,957 --> 00:02:00,425
Did I make you marry into this family?

30
00:02:00,449 --> 00:02:01,762
Why are you taking it out on me?

31
00:02:06,799 --> 00:02:08,141
Seriously.

32
00:02:20,885 --> 00:02:22,885
(My Wife)

33
00:02:25,325 --> 00:02:27,351
I guess I moved around too much.

34
00:02:27,376 --> 00:02:29,030
My whole body aches.

35
00:02:29,313 --> 00:02:30,545
I bet.

36
00:02:31,144 --> 00:02:35,403
Right. I haven't even thanked you
for helping with the wedding.

37
00:02:36,132 --> 00:02:38,568
We're friends.
You can buy me dinner sometime.

38
00:02:38,593 --> 00:02:40,745
I can buy you dinner anytime.

39
00:02:40,825 --> 00:02:42,078
When are you free?

40
00:02:42,252 --> 00:02:43,837
Me? Today.

41
00:02:44,536 --> 00:02:45,822
Is that too last-minute?

42
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:49,614
No. My plans got canceled today anyway.

43
00:02:49,882 --> 00:02:53,214
Really? Then how about
some pizza and beer?

44
00:02:54,053 --> 00:02:55,068
Sure. Sounds good.

45
00:02:58,265 --> 00:03:00,857
- Thank you.
- Looks delicious.

46
00:03:08,841 --> 00:03:10,535
This is good. It's been a while.

47
00:03:10,825 --> 00:03:12,172
When I got married,

48
00:03:12,385 --> 00:03:14,743
I thought it'd just be the two of us
having fun together.

49
00:03:15,972 --> 00:03:17,557
There's a lot to deal with
in marriage, right?

50
00:03:17,582 --> 00:03:18,991
And your brother's changed too.

51
00:03:19,322 --> 00:03:21,048
You're right. How did you know?

52
00:03:21,072 --> 00:03:23,237
How could I not? It's obvious.

53
00:03:25,332 --> 00:03:27,289
Yeong Ju gets angry
over the smallest things,

54
00:03:27,684 --> 00:03:29,489
and tells me not to say anything.

55
00:03:31,658 --> 00:03:34,378
Sometimes, silence helps more.

56
00:03:36,881 --> 00:03:37,890
But...

57
00:03:38,702 --> 00:03:41,320
Maestro, are you really
going to be a senior model?

58
00:03:42,154 --> 00:03:44,442
It's hard, but I'm having fun.

59
00:03:45,354 --> 00:03:46,535
That's amazing.

60
00:03:46,732 --> 00:03:49,576
I'll be cheering you on
as you take on this new challenge.

61
00:03:49,819 --> 00:03:51,449
Invite me to your first runway show.

62
00:03:51,626 --> 00:03:53,774
Why? So you can be my biggest fan again?

63
00:03:54,245 --> 00:03:55,657
Of course.

64
00:03:57,305 --> 00:03:58,878
- Here.
- Cheers.

65
00:04:00,216 --> 00:04:01,216
Wishing you success.

66
00:04:02,334 --> 00:04:03,995
Congratulations, Sa Bin.

67
00:04:04,512 --> 00:04:05,787
Thank you.

68
00:04:06,578 --> 00:04:09,197
- This is really good. Have some more.
- Okay.

69
00:04:10,877 --> 00:04:11,877
It's delicious.

70
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:19,593
Mom. Did you doze off?

71
00:04:20,585 --> 00:04:22,501
You must be tired
from taking care of the house all day.

72
00:04:23,058 --> 00:04:24,672
I called because I wanted
to hear your voice.

73
00:04:25,385 --> 00:04:26,385
Where's Sa Bin?

74
00:04:29,997 --> 00:04:31,085
A gathering of Korean medicine doctors?

75
00:04:32,351 --> 00:04:33,393
I see.

76
00:04:33,809 --> 00:04:35,401
Okay, my dear Yeong Ju.

77
00:04:35,841 --> 00:04:36,885
Get some rest.

78
00:05:30,242 --> 00:05:31,242
That's right.

79
00:05:31,936 --> 00:05:33,760
People don't change.

80
00:05:35,089 --> 00:05:36,343
What's that supposed to mean?

81
00:05:37,978 --> 00:05:39,537
Are you holding a grudge against my mom?

82
00:05:40,218 --> 00:05:42,560
- What?
- You dressed her up and married her off,

83
00:05:43,114 --> 00:05:44,797
and now you're after her husband again?

84
00:05:47,462 --> 00:05:49,849
- Are you crazy?
- You're the crazy one.

85
00:05:50,632 --> 00:05:52,220
Does stealing another woman's man
get you excited?

86
00:05:52,638 --> 00:05:54,187
Does it give you a dopamine rush?

87
00:06:00,938 --> 00:06:02,887
Why are you getting
between mom and Sa Bin?

88
00:06:02,889 --> 00:06:04,220
Why again?

89
00:06:05,925 --> 00:06:06,925
You...

90
00:06:07,628 --> 00:06:08,982
won't be forgiven this time.

91
00:06:09,712 --> 00:06:11,816
I will never forgive you.

92
00:06:23,365 --> 00:06:25,612
Hey, Na Ji Ni. Come out!

93
00:06:25,637 --> 00:06:27,375
- Hey, what's wrong with you?
- Come out!

94
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:30,015
- What's wrong? You're scaring her!
- What's going on?

95
00:06:30,183 --> 00:06:31,495
- What's wrong?
- Ji Ni.

96
00:06:32,097 --> 00:06:33,176
What?

97
00:06:33,521 --> 00:06:34,735
What's going on?

98
00:06:37,308 --> 00:06:38,651
Listen carefully, everyone.

99
00:06:40,152 --> 00:06:43,301
This woman and Im Sa Bin...

100
00:06:43,882 --> 00:06:45,989
were drinking together at the office.

101
00:06:46,562 --> 00:06:47,657
My mom...

102
00:06:48,325 --> 00:06:51,231
thought he was meeting with people
from the Korean Medicine Association.

103
00:06:51,913 --> 00:06:54,207
He lied to mom and met up with your mom.

104
00:06:54,558 --> 00:06:56,192
What do you think is going on here?

105
00:06:56,216 --> 00:06:57,216
Tell us.

106
00:06:57,589 --> 00:06:58,589
Mom...

107
00:06:58,742 --> 00:07:00,545
That's not true!

108
00:07:00,665 --> 00:07:04,193
Sa Bin told Yeong Ju
that he was drinking with me!

109
00:07:04,218 --> 00:07:06,287
My mom didn't know about it!

110
00:07:06,312 --> 00:07:08,334
I don't know about that,

111
00:07:08,359 --> 00:07:10,433
but we're friends, that's all.

112
00:07:10,458 --> 00:07:12,744
We've been friends
since before Yeong Ju married him!

113
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:14,232
Friends or not,

114
00:07:14,906 --> 00:07:16,930
you have a history of this!

115
00:07:17,211 --> 00:07:18,964
And the woman involved is my mom!

116
00:07:19,231 --> 00:07:21,124
Then you should've been even more careful!

117
00:07:22,044 --> 00:07:23,873
Why do you lose your mind
whenever you see another woman's man...

118
00:07:23,898 --> 00:07:26,114
and throw yourself at him?

119
00:07:26,811 --> 00:07:28,309
Does breaking up someone else's family...

120
00:07:28,333 --> 00:07:29,791
make you feel important?

121
00:07:29,792 --> 00:07:32,541
Seriously, do you think
you can say whatever you want?

122
00:07:32,542 --> 00:07:34,501
Mom!

123
00:07:34,910 --> 00:07:35,950
Mom!

124
00:07:35,951 --> 00:07:37,510
I'm not letting this happen twice.

125
00:07:38,853 --> 00:07:39,853
Are you okay?

126
00:07:42,038 --> 00:07:43,510
That's not what happened.

127
00:07:44,147 --> 00:07:46,027
They've known each other
since I was little.

128
00:07:46,052 --> 00:07:48,020
They used to see each other
with my dad too.

129
00:07:48,045 --> 00:07:49,805
But they met alone this time.

130
00:07:50,151 --> 00:07:52,207
And they lied about it!

131
00:07:52,599 --> 00:07:53,995
Does denying it make it okay?

132
00:07:54,901 --> 00:07:56,041
You're just like her.

133
00:07:56,458 --> 00:07:58,138
Look at what you've been doing lately!

134
00:07:58,169 --> 00:08:01,005
- You're just like your mom!
- You...

135
00:08:01,047 --> 00:08:04,054
Apologize!

136
00:08:04,079 --> 00:08:06,560
How dare you talk to Ji Ni like that?

137
00:08:06,585 --> 00:08:09,201
How dare you cause a scene here?

138
00:08:09,402 --> 00:08:10,402
That's right!

139
00:08:11,651 --> 00:08:14,119
I'm just like my mom. I'm her daughter.

140
00:08:14,144 --> 00:08:15,307
Isn't that only natural?

141
00:08:15,792 --> 00:08:17,920
You're just like dad too.

142
00:08:19,541 --> 00:08:21,791
- What did you say?
- How much do you look down on us...

143
00:08:21,793 --> 00:08:23,141
to treat us like this?

144
00:08:23,414 --> 00:08:24,414
What?

145
00:08:24,831 --> 00:08:26,868
You think she goes after
other women's men?

146
00:08:27,543 --> 00:08:29,588
How can you say something so cruel?

147
00:08:32,697 --> 00:08:33,697
Enough.

148
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:35,555
Get out.

149
00:08:36,809 --> 00:08:37,985
We're strangers.

150
00:08:39,105 --> 00:08:42,172
Don't call me your brother
when you're out in public.

151
00:08:42,977 --> 00:08:44,247
You're not my sister.

152
00:08:44,545 --> 00:08:45,847
I won't call you my brother either.

153
00:08:46,605 --> 00:08:48,066
Why are you forcing the issue again?

154
00:08:48,091 --> 00:08:49,480
I heard everything.

155
00:08:51,412 --> 00:08:53,051
You're just as good at denying it.

156
00:08:53,884 --> 00:08:54,884
Seung Hyun.

157
00:08:55,457 --> 00:08:56,853
Let's live apart from them now.

158
00:08:57,792 --> 00:08:59,205
We've put up with enough.

159
00:09:06,638 --> 00:09:08,045
- Tomorrow morning...
- No.

160
00:09:08,455 --> 00:09:09,599
We're leaving now.

161
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:11,099
I don't want to stay here anymore.

162
00:09:11,591 --> 00:09:12,937
Mom, come inside. Pack your things.

163
00:09:13,456 --> 00:09:15,379
- Ji Ni.
- Let's go anywhere.

164
00:09:15,404 --> 00:09:16,780
Why can't we?

165
00:09:30,891 --> 00:09:33,672
Where are you going this late?

166
00:09:33,937 --> 00:09:35,530
Ji Ni, I didn't do that.

167
00:09:35,625 --> 00:09:38,647
So why should we leave
when we did nothing wrong?

168
00:09:38,672 --> 00:09:40,207
They told us to leave!

169
00:09:40,393 --> 00:09:41,557
I don't want to stay here.

170
00:09:41,696 --> 00:09:43,741
I really don't!

171
00:10:04,938 --> 00:10:06,439
Are you hurt anywhere?

172
00:10:06,441 --> 00:10:07,739
You fell earlier.

173
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:11,884
I can't tell yet.

174
00:10:11,909 --> 00:10:13,620
I'm still in shock.

175
00:10:15,951 --> 00:10:17,645
Thanks for believing me.

176
00:10:18,919 --> 00:10:20,878
After your dad left, things were hard,

177
00:10:21,096 --> 00:10:23,435
but I thought of you
and kept myself together.

178
00:10:23,776 --> 00:10:25,687
I'm sorry I put you through this again.

179
00:10:25,956 --> 00:10:27,222
Exactly.

180
00:10:27,638 --> 00:10:30,537
I told you not to see that doctor.

181
00:10:30,852 --> 00:10:33,091
Nobody knows how you feel.
They only judge what they see.

182
00:10:33,823 --> 00:10:34,823
And...

183
00:10:36,312 --> 00:10:37,957
you have a history of this, Mom.

184
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:43,205
We still don't deserve to be kicked out.

185
00:10:44,744 --> 00:10:46,472
Look at this.

186
00:10:50,156 --> 00:10:51,211
(Agreement. I, Cha Seung Hyun, acknowledge
Ji Ni's marrow donation to O Reum.)

187
00:10:51,236 --> 00:10:52,251
(I promise not to disrespect
either her or her mom.)

188
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:53,308
(If I break this agreement, I will pay
them 100,000 dollars to move out.)

189
00:10:53,605 --> 00:10:54,757
What's this?

190
00:10:55,693 --> 00:10:58,103
I got Seung Hyun to sign this agreement.

191
00:10:58,512 --> 00:11:01,298
What did he say when you donated
your marrow to O Reum?

192
00:11:01,345 --> 00:11:04,589
He needed you then,
so he promised to do anything.

193
00:11:04,793 --> 00:11:07,882
Then he started objecting
to everything we did.

194
00:11:08,059 --> 00:11:09,824
Did he have to hold
the house over our heads?

195
00:11:10,019 --> 00:11:12,507
He was so petty, so I made him sign this.

196
00:11:14,778 --> 00:11:16,795
- Mom...
- I did the right thing, didn't I?

197
00:11:16,853 --> 00:11:18,335
When Seung Hyun saw us leaving,

198
00:11:18,466 --> 00:11:20,985
he must've panicked.

199
00:11:21,425 --> 00:11:24,132
Let's take the 100,000 dollars
and get our own place.

200
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,548
It'll cover the deposit.

201
00:11:25,572 --> 00:11:28,053
If we both work,
we can cover the monthly rent.

202
00:11:31,033 --> 00:11:33,353
Hey!

203
00:11:33,378 --> 00:11:35,974
Do you know how I managed
to get that agreement?

204
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:38,664
Why would we take this money?

205
00:11:39,132 --> 00:11:40,387
The price of O Reum's life?

206
00:11:41,237 --> 00:11:42,487
That's ridiculous.

207
00:11:42,794 --> 00:11:44,184
Did I sell my bone marrow?

208
00:11:44,209 --> 00:11:46,289
This is exactly why you drive me crazy!

209
00:11:46,304 --> 00:11:49,278
Na Ji Ni! The world is all about money!

210
00:11:49,289 --> 00:11:50,628
Not this money.

211
00:11:51,278 --> 00:11:53,487
If you're innocent, prove it properly.

212
00:11:54,225 --> 00:11:55,505
If you accept this,

213
00:11:56,231 --> 00:11:57,757
I'm done with you too.

214
00:11:58,119 --> 00:12:00,824
I'll go somewhere no one knows me
and live on my own.

215
00:12:01,062 --> 00:12:02,124
It's up to you.

216
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:05,951
You little brat.

217
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:12,539
That brat.

218
00:12:13,241 --> 00:12:14,996
Listen to her talking big.

219
00:12:15,014 --> 00:12:18,497
We should at least get enough for a house.
Why leave empty-handed?

220
00:12:22,918 --> 00:12:26,547
I heard your parents run a guesthouse.

221
00:12:27,139 --> 00:12:28,526
Are all the rooms booked?

222
00:12:28,874 --> 00:12:32,676
Would you have a room for my mom and me?

223
00:12:33,843 --> 00:12:36,305
- We're in a difficult situation...
- Okay. I'll handle it.

224
00:12:36,576 --> 00:12:38,449
- Where are you right now?
- At the studio.

225
00:12:39,449 --> 00:12:40,449
Okay.

226
00:13:03,198 --> 00:13:04,270
They left.

227
00:13:05,028 --> 00:13:06,385
Was what you said earlier true?

228
00:13:06,692 --> 00:13:07,951
About Sa Bin and that woman.

229
00:13:09,754 --> 00:13:10,754
Yes.

230
00:13:11,158 --> 00:13:12,767
They lied to mom and met in secret.

231
00:13:12,852 --> 00:13:14,375
Do you know how affectionate they were?

232
00:13:14,557 --> 00:13:15,860
If I'd had my way...

233
00:13:16,042 --> 00:13:18,810
I'd have barged in and gone after him too.

234
00:13:19,363 --> 00:13:20,731
But I held back because of mom.

235
00:13:23,245 --> 00:13:25,350
Why is mom seeing a man like that?

236
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:27,347
Why is she involved with that woman again?

237
00:13:27,372 --> 00:13:29,575
You did the right thing
not going after him.

238
00:13:30,696 --> 00:13:33,387
But I'm not sure it was right
to throw them out like that.

239
00:13:33,412 --> 00:13:34,613
So should we keep living with them?

240
00:13:35,178 --> 00:13:36,654
We should've done this long ago.

241
00:13:38,592 --> 00:13:40,113
That foolish Yeong Ju.

242
00:13:40,507 --> 00:13:42,276
She has terrible taste in men.

243
00:13:42,292 --> 00:13:45,712
I almost lost it when I saw them together.

244
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,308
I see.

245
00:13:51,491 --> 00:13:52,758
And what's this
about her calling you her brother?

246
00:13:52,783 --> 00:13:56,004
Apparently, Ji Ni goes around
calling us her brothers.

247
00:13:56,234 --> 00:13:57,234
Can you believe that?

248
00:13:57,804 --> 00:13:59,377
Look at how she treats us at home.

249
00:13:59,402 --> 00:14:00,592
Hard to believe, isn't it?

250
00:14:00,892 --> 00:14:02,396
That's how two-faced she is.

251
00:14:02,421 --> 00:14:04,006
She's no different from her mom.

252
00:14:25,638 --> 00:14:27,185
Yeong Ju.

253
00:14:31,031 --> 00:14:32,098
Bean sprout soup?

254
00:14:33,098 --> 00:14:34,545
Because you drank last night.

255
00:14:35,079 --> 00:14:36,590
I'm touched.

256
00:14:37,238 --> 00:14:40,812
I was already feeling queasy.

257
00:14:42,192 --> 00:14:44,045
What if someone comes out and sees us?

258
00:14:44,445 --> 00:14:46,278
So what? We're married.

259
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:48,991
Why did you drink so much
when you can't handle alcohol?

260
00:14:48,993 --> 00:14:51,138
Maestro can really hold her liquor.

261
00:14:51,158 --> 00:14:53,439
She kept raising her glass,
so I had to keep up.

262
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:54,963
Maestro?

263
00:14:56,098 --> 00:14:58,290
You drank with Se Ri yesterday?

264
00:14:58,538 --> 00:15:00,778
You said you were meeting people
from the Korean Medicine Association.

265
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,158
The meeting got canceled.

266
00:15:02,267 --> 00:15:04,521
Right. I tried to tell you yesterday,

267
00:15:04,523 --> 00:15:06,538
but you didn't answer my call.

268
00:15:06,777 --> 00:15:08,140
Why did you go to bed so early?

269
00:15:16,105 --> 00:15:17,140
Yeong Ju.

270
00:15:18,499 --> 00:15:19,499
Yeong Ju!

271
00:15:27,018 --> 00:15:30,031
Yeong Ju, what's wrong?

272
00:15:31,939 --> 00:15:33,912
Why did you catch it? Let me hit you!

273
00:15:34,811 --> 00:15:36,381
Why are you angry?

274
00:15:37,065 --> 00:15:38,900
I honestly don't understand.

275
00:15:39,712 --> 00:15:41,121
As for the maestro...

276
00:15:41,694 --> 00:15:44,001
I knew her long before I met you.

277
00:15:44,002 --> 00:15:46,592
Romantic feelings?
I've never had any. I mean it.

278
00:15:46,938 --> 00:15:48,265
We're just friends.

279
00:15:48,806 --> 00:15:50,929
Why are you so sensitive?

280
00:15:50,930 --> 00:15:51,930
Sensitive?

281
00:15:53,504 --> 00:15:56,405
If you really don't understand,
just memorize it!

282
00:15:58,712 --> 00:16:00,372
What's with that look?

283
00:16:00,565 --> 00:16:02,671
I was humiliated at home,

284
00:16:02,892 --> 00:16:04,689
and you were drinking with Se Ri?

285
00:16:04,690 --> 00:16:05,690
Humiliated?

286
00:16:06,065 --> 00:16:07,481
Did Sun Kyung mistreat you again?

287
00:16:07,652 --> 00:16:08,813
I swear...

288
00:16:10,169 --> 00:16:12,331
You idiot!

289
00:16:12,352 --> 00:16:14,521
Why don't you understand me?

290
00:16:15,369 --> 00:16:17,113
What's gotten into you?

291
00:16:21,445 --> 00:16:23,810
The first episode got amazing ratings!

292
00:16:24,792 --> 00:16:27,931
Do Hee's gaining followers like crazy!

293
00:16:27,998 --> 00:16:30,198
See? I told you it would be a hit.

294
00:16:30,738 --> 00:16:32,275
Now you're a variety show director.

295
00:16:32,402 --> 00:16:33,411
Just follow my lead.

296
00:16:33,445 --> 00:16:35,212
I'm glad all that hard work paid off.

297
00:16:38,338 --> 00:16:40,570
Ma'am, what brings you here so early?

298
00:16:40,971 --> 00:16:42,565
- Our meeting...
- I know.

299
00:16:43,125 --> 00:16:45,445
I need to speak with Director Cha first.

300
00:16:45,625 --> 00:16:48,369
Ms. Song, could you give us a minute?

301
00:16:49,497 --> 00:16:50,497
Okay.

302
00:16:57,951 --> 00:16:59,543
What brings you here so early?

303
00:16:59,545 --> 00:17:02,799
Besides what you say you saw,
what evidence do you have?

304
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,948
What? You're saying Ji Ni is like me?

305
00:17:07,438 --> 00:17:09,673
I'll be fuming over this all night.

306
00:17:09,865 --> 00:17:12,700
What proof do you have
to say something like that?

307
00:17:12,852 --> 00:17:15,096
What are you talking about?
What exactly did you see?

308
00:17:15,145 --> 00:17:16,394
What did Ji Ni do?

309
00:17:16,885 --> 00:17:19,045
She's seeing the man Do Hee is dating.

310
00:17:19,805 --> 00:17:21,278
I've seen them together several times.

311
00:17:22,398 --> 00:17:24,151
That brat Do Hee again?

312
00:17:24,798 --> 00:17:26,190
So...

313
00:17:26,357 --> 00:17:29,460
Are you saying Ji Ni loves Ji Hu?

314
00:17:29,555 --> 00:17:30,700
Are they dating?

315
00:17:31,209 --> 00:17:33,912
- Did they break up because of Ji Ni?
- That's what she says.

316
00:17:34,452 --> 00:17:36,131
You did the same thing at first.

317
00:17:36,541 --> 00:17:37,963
You were my mom's junior.

318
00:17:37,965 --> 00:17:39,642
Then you betrayed her...

319
00:17:39,990 --> 00:17:42,950
left my brother waiting for dad,
and destroyed our home!

320
00:17:43,978 --> 00:17:44,991
You think I don't know that trick?

321
00:17:44,993 --> 00:17:47,631
Stop dragging up the past.
It was 30 years ago! I'm sick of it!

322
00:17:47,952 --> 00:17:50,267
Fine, I've made that mistake before.

323
00:17:50,425 --> 00:17:53,829
But does that give you the right
to accuse Ji Ni in front of me?

324
00:17:53,831 --> 00:17:56,031
Like mother, like daughter!

325
00:18:01,351 --> 00:18:03,351
Seriously...

326
00:18:06,072 --> 00:18:09,384
I've heard and seen enough.

327
00:18:10,277 --> 00:18:11,937
That's why I'm saying it.

328
00:18:11,939 --> 00:18:13,630
You already insulted me,

329
00:18:13,931 --> 00:18:16,245
and now you're accusing Ji Ni too?

330
00:18:16,605 --> 00:18:18,469
I'll never forgive you.

331
00:18:18,672 --> 00:18:21,952
You'd better apologize properly.

332
00:18:21,954 --> 00:18:23,900
Who do you think you're scaring
by saying you won't forgive me?

333
00:18:24,638 --> 00:18:26,679
A daughter takes after her mom.
Who else would she take after?

334
00:18:27,045 --> 00:18:28,769
That's what she said yesterday.

335
00:18:29,745 --> 00:18:33,408
I didn't realize you'd keep bringing up
what happened 30 years ago.

336
00:18:33,773 --> 00:18:35,504
But we're family, after all.

337
00:18:35,858 --> 00:18:38,408
Seeing how well she treats you all,

338
00:18:39,171 --> 00:18:42,098
I tried not to let my own selfishness
ruin this relationship.

339
00:18:42,216 --> 00:18:44,865
I regret being so careful now.

340
00:18:45,085 --> 00:18:46,842
I felt the same way!

341
00:18:47,838 --> 00:18:49,925
We weren't especially close,
but I never shut you out either.

342
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:52,600
I just let things be.

343
00:18:52,885 --> 00:18:55,765
And somehow, we even ended up
living under the same roof.

344
00:18:57,585 --> 00:18:59,931
Do you know how shocked I was yesterday?

345
00:19:00,612 --> 00:19:03,658
Good thing I saw it myself.
If my mom had seen it,

346
00:19:04,315 --> 00:19:05,502
she would've collapsed again!

347
00:19:06,918 --> 00:19:11,113
I'll meet her and Sa Bin
and prove it to you,

348
00:19:11,414 --> 00:19:13,631
so just you wait.

349
00:19:31,511 --> 00:19:32,721
Did you sleep well last night?

350
00:19:34,378 --> 00:19:35,704
Was everything comfortable?

351
00:19:35,864 --> 00:19:36,864
Yes.

352
00:19:37,305 --> 00:19:40,940
I'm really grateful you came right away
when I called you so late last night.

353
00:19:41,325 --> 00:19:42,567
How much is it for one night?

354
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:44,978
- I'll pay you.
- No, it's fine.

355
00:19:44,980 --> 00:19:46,998
I heard your parents run this place.

356
00:19:47,223 --> 00:19:48,992
My mom told me to make sure I paid.

357
00:19:49,115 --> 00:19:50,905
You're going to hurt my feelings
if you keep this up.

358
00:19:50,998 --> 00:19:52,959
If I ever end up out on the street,
you'd help me, right?

359
00:19:54,915 --> 00:19:56,104
Okay.

360
00:19:56,232 --> 00:19:58,338
I'll repay your kindness someday.

361
00:19:58,425 --> 00:19:59,888
Yeah. Do that.

362
00:20:00,792 --> 00:20:01,977
Is the coffee ready?

363
00:20:02,123 --> 00:20:04,352
Yes, almost.

364
00:20:12,025 --> 00:20:13,131
It's ready.

365
00:20:13,356 --> 00:20:14,798
We're having a team dinner tonight, right?

366
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:16,725
Yes. Think about what you want to eat.

367
00:20:17,572 --> 00:20:18,985
I brought the CEO's card.

368
00:20:21,805 --> 00:20:25,040
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

369
00:20:26,731 --> 00:20:27,813
Thank you.

370
00:20:28,557 --> 00:20:29,825
Did you watch "Love in Zip" yesterday?

371
00:20:29,827 --> 00:20:32,085
It was pretty good, right?
It's the hottest show right now.

372
00:20:32,087 --> 00:20:34,905
My friends are going crazy
over how pretty Do Hee is.

373
00:20:36,105 --> 00:20:39,465
So I just said,
"Her personality, not so much."

374
00:20:40,369 --> 00:20:42,078
She said she works in publishing.

375
00:20:42,145 --> 00:20:43,594
Can you believe that?

376
00:20:44,496 --> 00:20:46,425
Shouldn't she have introduced herself
as a professional thief?

377
00:20:46,518 --> 00:20:47,974
She's the best thief in Korea.

378
00:20:47,976 --> 00:20:50,325
Exactly. Seriously!

379
00:20:50,352 --> 00:20:51,960
Should I put it all over the internet?

380
00:20:55,895 --> 00:20:56,915
Look at this.

381
00:20:57,052 --> 00:20:59,040
She posted something on social media.

382
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:01,038
- It's about the two of you.
- What?

383
00:21:03,958 --> 00:21:05,541
Is she seriously out of her mind?

384
00:21:13,878 --> 00:21:15,550
Hi, everyone. It's Do Hee.

385
00:21:16,131 --> 00:21:19,569
Thank you all for your love and support
for "Love in Zip."

386
00:21:19,998 --> 00:21:22,606
I said I worked for a publishing company,

387
00:21:22,725 --> 00:21:23,969
but I don't anymore.

388
00:21:24,338 --> 00:21:26,338
My fiancé kicked me out...

389
00:21:26,340 --> 00:21:29,511
and brought in the woman
he was cheating with to take my place.

390
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:33,611
That woman is actually
someone I went to middle school with.

391
00:21:33,732 --> 00:21:35,205
Funny how life works, right?

392
00:21:36,151 --> 00:21:39,671
Anyway, I'm rooting for Im Ji Hu
and Na Ji Ni.

393
00:21:40,283 --> 00:21:42,082
Go, The Captain's Library Publishing!

394
00:21:42,596 --> 00:21:45,049
I hope you'll all support me too.

395
00:21:51,132 --> 00:21:52,598
How could she lie like this...

396
00:21:59,805 --> 00:22:01,544
Yes, this is
The Captain's Library Publishing.

397
00:22:02,152 --> 00:22:04,243
No, that's not true.

398
00:22:05,197 --> 00:22:06,521
Yes. Okay.

399
00:22:12,852 --> 00:22:13,852
Don't answer it.

400
00:22:14,789 --> 00:22:16,198
Unplug the phone for now.

401
00:22:17,438 --> 00:22:20,419
And make sure you explain the truth
to anyone who asks you directly.

402
00:22:21,138 --> 00:22:23,394
If these rumors keep spreading,
it'll hurt our publishing company.

403
00:22:53,498 --> 00:22:54,569
What are you listening to?

404
00:22:54,825 --> 00:22:55,952
A song I wrote.

405
00:22:56,851 --> 00:22:57,851
Want to hear it?

406
00:23:19,665 --> 00:23:20,748
It's nice.

407
00:23:21,276 --> 00:23:22,317
What's it called?

408
00:23:23,345 --> 00:23:24,850
"You are My One Reason."

409
00:23:30,838 --> 00:23:31,981
Ji Ni.

410
00:23:32,684 --> 00:23:35,190
- I'm really sorry.
- Don't apologize.

411
00:23:35,918 --> 00:23:37,085
I'm okay.

412
00:23:38,131 --> 00:23:40,496
We escaped from the storage room.

413
00:23:42,038 --> 00:23:44,091
So don't worry about it, Ji Hu.

414
00:23:47,298 --> 00:23:48,404
I enjoyed it.

415
00:24:00,585 --> 00:24:01,785
I'm not okay.

416
00:24:21,018 --> 00:24:22,205
Mother.

417
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:25,231
I'm so glad you asked me to come.

418
00:24:27,158 --> 00:24:29,405
I'm not in the mood to smile,
so let's get straight to the point.

419
00:24:29,666 --> 00:24:32,299
What on earth are you doing?

420
00:24:32,756 --> 00:24:33,756
What?

421
00:24:35,552 --> 00:24:38,732
What's this post you put online?

422
00:24:40,305 --> 00:24:43,538
You're making Ji Hu look like
he was two-timing you?

423
00:24:44,252 --> 00:24:47,343
Look, I may have taken your side,

424
00:24:47,884 --> 00:24:50,527
but I don't even remember when he said...

425
00:24:50,536 --> 00:24:51,900
he wanted to break up with you.

426
00:24:52,258 --> 00:24:53,683
So how was he two-timing you?

427
00:24:53,832 --> 00:24:55,078
Or leaving you for someone else?

428
00:24:55,195 --> 00:24:57,645
Look at you.
You're ruining his reputation.

429
00:24:58,271 --> 00:25:00,884
People have been calling nonstop.

430
00:25:00,958 --> 00:25:01,958
Delete it. Now.

431
00:25:02,365 --> 00:25:04,390
- I won't.
- Hey!

432
00:25:04,392 --> 00:25:06,712
Then you should've kept your son in line.

433
00:25:07,025 --> 00:25:08,712
You keep saying you'll handle it,

434
00:25:09,025 --> 00:25:10,832
but what have you actually done?

435
00:25:11,805 --> 00:25:13,593
Ji Ni's back at the publishing company,

436
00:25:14,491 --> 00:25:16,132
and he's gotten everything
thanks to my dad.

437
00:25:16,134 --> 00:25:17,624
So who's the one who betrayed whom?

438
00:25:18,230 --> 00:25:19,253
Me?

439
00:25:19,602 --> 00:25:20,649
It's you.

440
00:25:20,651 --> 00:25:21,980
Unbelievable!

441
00:25:22,798 --> 00:25:24,616
Hey! Let's get our facts straight.

442
00:25:24,618 --> 00:25:26,833
Before that Ji Ni girl ever showed up,

443
00:25:26,835 --> 00:25:29,506
he had already told you he wanted
to break up.

444
00:25:30,658 --> 00:25:34,361
He rejected you regardless of Ji Ni.

445
00:25:34,363 --> 00:25:36,605
No. It's because of her.

446
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:38,880
Ma'am,

447
00:25:39,025 --> 00:25:41,586
you're the one who's lying here.

448
00:25:41,820 --> 00:25:43,220
What? "Ma'am?"

449
00:25:45,312 --> 00:25:47,363
- Take the post down.
- No.

450
00:25:47,365 --> 00:25:49,795
I was dumped for Na Ji Ni.
That's what happened.

451
00:25:50,332 --> 00:25:51,772
That's how I see it.

452
00:25:52,418 --> 00:25:54,568
What's wrong with posting...

453
00:25:54,756 --> 00:25:56,203
- my opinion online?
- Take it down!

454
00:25:56,205 --> 00:25:58,763
No! I won't. I'm going to keep going.

455
00:25:58,765 --> 00:25:59,972
I told you I would.

456
00:26:00,838 --> 00:26:02,949
I've got even more followers now.

457
00:26:03,938 --> 00:26:05,520
This is going to hurt...

458
00:26:06,101 --> 00:26:07,977
you and Na Ji Ni.

459
00:26:08,118 --> 00:26:10,345
I've told you countless times
that I wanted to break up.

460
00:26:10,472 --> 00:26:14,895
The moment I found out you were a bully
in school, I couldn't trust you anymore.

461
00:26:14,897 --> 00:26:19,092
We broke up because you lied.
It had nothing to do with her.

462
00:26:20,791 --> 00:26:22,316
We can't fix this anymore.

463
00:26:23,359 --> 00:26:24,460
I know.

464
00:26:25,712 --> 00:26:28,038
And I'm not going to keep
begging you anymore.

465
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:29,139
Then why are you doing this?

466
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:31,530
Because it's fun.

467
00:26:32,948 --> 00:26:34,830
Because it'll hurt you and her.

468
00:26:34,902 --> 00:26:36,218
Have you lost your mind?

469
00:26:39,878 --> 00:26:41,668
What on earth are you doing? Give it back!

470
00:26:41,942 --> 00:26:42,942
Give it back!

471
00:26:44,672 --> 00:26:46,518
Fine. I'll just post it again.

472
00:26:46,998 --> 00:26:48,909
I can buy ten more phones if I want.

473
00:26:48,970 --> 00:26:49,970
You know that.

474
00:26:50,518 --> 00:26:52,391
I took Ji Ni's tablet
and gave her the new ones.

475
00:26:53,458 --> 00:26:54,871
Was that really you?

476
00:26:54,891 --> 00:26:57,465
- Stay out of this.
- What?

477
00:27:09,885 --> 00:27:11,707
You can't stop me.

478
00:27:12,361 --> 00:27:13,361
Give it up.

479
00:27:31,562 --> 00:27:34,896
(Family Register)

480
00:27:34,898 --> 00:27:37,030
- The general wants to see you.
- You've got to be kidding me.

481
00:27:37,077 --> 00:27:38,437
Is this the military or what?

482
00:27:38,439 --> 00:27:40,131
- That's not fair.
- What's not fair?

483
00:27:40,151 --> 00:27:41,616
Do you realize how much trouble...

484
00:27:41,618 --> 00:27:43,533
your thoughtless actions have caused?

485
00:27:43,534 --> 00:27:45,716
Make things right.
Live apart if you must, but not like this.

486
00:27:45,718 --> 00:27:46,985
Now that it's come to this,
just go separate ways.

487
00:27:46,986 --> 00:27:48,990
I was passing by and saw you here,
so I thought I'd stop by.

488
00:27:48,992 --> 00:27:51,806
- Just give it a little more time.
- The magic of waiting...

489
00:27:52,007 --> 00:27:53,623
I know how you feel. I'll handle it.

490
00:27:53,625 --> 00:27:55,062
I'll protect you.

491
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:56,512
Will you date me?

492
00:27:57,733 --> 00:27:59,733
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
